---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const schema = `[{
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": ["LocalBusiness", "RoofingContractor"],
    "name": "Happy Roof LLC",
    "url": "https://happyroof.com",
    "telephone": "+1-813-595-7663",
    "email": "info@happyroof.com",
    "description": "Tampa Bay roof repair contractor offering emergency leak repair, storm damage repair, shingle replacement, and flashing repair. FL License #CCC1337380.",
    "image": "/Brand%20Assets/Happy%20Roof%20Logo.jpeg",
    "logo": "/Brand%20Assets/Happy%20Roof%20Logo.jpeg",
    "address": {
      "@type": "PostalAddress",
      "streetAddress": "141 Stevens Ave #12","addressLocality": "Oldsmar",
      "addressRegion": "FL","postalCode": "34677","addressCountry": "US"
    },
    "hasCredential": "Florida Roofing Contractor License #CCC1337380",
    "dateModified": "2026-04-25"
  },{
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "FAQPage",
    "mainEntity": [
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "How quickly can Happy Roof respond to an emergency roof repair?",
        "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "Happy Roof offers a 48-hour emergency response for roof repairs in Tampa Bay. If your roof is actively leaking or has sustained storm damage, call (813) 595-7663 immediately. We can typically have a crew on-site within 24 to 48 hours to tarp, patch, or stabilize your roof and prevent further interior damage." }
      },
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "Does Happy Roof help with roof insurance claims?",
        "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "Yes. Happy Roof provides full insurance claim assistance for storm damage and other covered roof repairs. We document all damage with photos and detailed reports, meet with your insurance adjuster on-site, and help ensure your claim is processed fairly. We work with all major Florida homeowners insurance carriers." }
      },
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "How do I know if my roof needs a repair or a full replacement?",
        "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "Generally, if the damage is isolated to a small area (missing shingles, a single leak point, damaged flashing around one penetration), a repair is the most cost-effective solution. If your roof is over 15-20 years old, has widespread damage, multiple leak points, or significant decking deterioration, a full replacement is usually the better long-term investment. Happy Roof provides honest assessments. We will never recommend a replacement when a repair will do." }
      },
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "Do you offer a warranty on roof repairs?",
        "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "Yes. Qualifying repairs come with our written workmanship warranty of up to 15 years, which covers our labor and installation. Not every repair qualifies at the same level; for example, emergency tarping is different from a permanent shingle or flashing repair, but we will always tell you exactly what is covered before work starts." }
      },
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "How much does a roof repair cost in Tampa Bay?",
        "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "Minor repairs like replacing a few shingles or sealing a small leak typically run $300 to $800. More involved repairs (e.g., flashing replacement, multiple leak sources, storm damage restoration) typically fall between $1,000 and $3,500 or more depending on scope. Happy Roof provides free inspections and written estimates with no hidden fees. Call (813) 595-7663 for a personalized quote." }
      },
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "Can you repair a TPO or flat roof?",
        "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "Yes. Happy Roof repairs all flat roof systems including TPO, EPDM, modified bitumen, and built-up roofing. Common flat roof repairs include seam re-welding, puncture patching, flashing replacement, and ponding water correction. We also repair leaks around rooftop HVAC units, pipes, and drains. Call (813) 595-7663 for a free inspection." }
      },
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "What can I do to prevent roof leaks?",
        "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "Most roof leaks start in relatively predictable places. Inspecting your flashing twice a year, particularly around any chimneys, vents, skylights, and places where the roof meets the wall, can help you catch a lot of problems on the early side. Other efforts include: keep gutters clear to prevent water from backing up under the drip edge; trim branches that hang over the roof to reduce debris and potential abrasion; and check for lifted or missing shingles after any named storm to have a chance of addressing smaller issues before they become more serious ones. Plus, a professional inspection once a year, which we offer for free, is the single most effective thing you can do to stay ahead of it. Call (813) 595-7663." }
      },
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "Which roof repairs are safe to DIY, and when should I call a pro?",
        "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "Roof access is where most DIY roofing goes wrong. The CDC documents over 150,000 ladder-fall ER visits every year in the US, and Florida shingle heat plus tile fragility make walking a roof more dangerous than most homeowners realize. SAFE TO DIY (from the ground or an eave-anchored ladder only, never the roof plane): (1) Clear gutters and downspouts, the #1 cause of hidden leaks; a gutter scoop and a stable ladder against the eave is all you need. (2) Trim overhanging branches with a pole saw from the ground to keep limbs off the shingles and reduce debris. (3) Photograph the roof after every named storm from the ground, same angles, in the same order. Insurance loves date-stamped 'before' photos. (4) Attic check twice a year: flashlight, look for water stains on the underside of decking, daylight through nail holes, wet insulation, or musty smell. (5) Reseal exposed sealant on ground-accessible sections only, like a first-floor porch roof, using a shingle-safe sealant. Never attempt from a ladder above 10 feet or on the main roof plane. CALL A LICENSED ROOFER FOR: any leak repair (80% of leaks start at flashing, and DIY caulking hides the source while the deck rots underneath); any shingle or tile replacement on a walkable roof; any work around chimneys, skylights, plumbing vents, or valleys (all warranty-sensitive); any tile repair (cracked tiles under foot are the injury pattern we see most); storm damage inspection with insurance implications (an untrained eye misses hail bruising and wind-lifted seals that a licensed inspector documents for a claim); and any repair on a two-story home or roof pitch above 6:12. Rule of thumb: if the fix requires walking the roof plane, you need a licensed roofer. Happy Roof offers free inspections at (813) 595-7663, one call saves a fall." }
      }
    ]
  },{
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "Service",
    "serviceType": "Roof Repair",
    "provider": { "@type": "RoofingContractor", "name": "Happy Roof LLC", "telephone": "+1-813-595-7663", "url": "https://happyroof.com" },
    "areaServed": { "@type": "State", "name": "Florida" },
    "description": "Professional roof repair services in Tampa Bay including emergency leak repair, storm damage repair, shingle replacement, flashing repair, and insurance claim assistance. 48-hour emergency response. 15-year warranty option on qualifying repairs."
  },{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"BreadcrumbList","itemListElement":[{"@type":"ListItem","position":1,"name":"Home","item":"https://happyroof.com/"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":2,"name":"Services","item":"https://happyroof.com/services"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":3,"name":"Roof Repair","item":"https://happyroof.com/roof-repair"}]},{
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "Service",
    "name": "Roof Repair",
    "description": "Professional roof repair services in Tampa Bay including leak repair, shingle replacement, flashing repair, and emergency tarping.",
    "provider": {"@type": "RoofingContractor", "name": "Happy Roof LLC"},
    "areaServed": {"@type": "City", "name": "Tampa Bay"},
    "offers": {
      "@type": "Offer",
      "priceRange": "$350 - $1,500",
      "priceCurrency": "USD"
    },
    "termsOfService": "Up to 15-year workmanship warranty on qualifying repairs"
  }]`;
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Roof Repair Services in Tampa Bay | Happy Roof"
  description="Is your roof leaking? Was it recently damaged in a storm? We offer roof repair services throughout the Tampa Bay area. Call today for a free estimate."
  canonical="https://happyroof.com/roof-repair"
  ogTitle="Roof Repair Tampa Bay | Emergency Leak & Storm Damage | Happy Roof"
  ogDescription="Fast, honest roof repairs in Tampa Bay. 48hr emergency response. Leak detection, shingle replacement, storm damage. 15-year warranty option on qualifying repairs."
  schema={schema}
>

<style is:inline>
.check-dot{width:20px;height:20px;border-radius:50%;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;background:rgba(230,168,23,.1);flex-shrink:0;margin-top:.15rem}
    .step-num{width:48px;height:48px;border-radius:14px;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;background:rgba(230,168,23,.1);font-family:'Barlow Condensed',sans-serif;font-weight:800;font-size:1.25rem;color:#E6A817;flex-shrink:0}
</style>

<!-- PAGE HERO -->
<section class="pt-32 pb-20 relative overflow-hidden" style="background:#F5F5F5;border-bottom:1px solid #E5E5E5">
  <div class="hero-photo-bg" style="background-image:url('/Brand%20Assets/Photos/architectural-shingle-roof-tampa-bay.jpg')"></div>
  <div class="hero-photo-overlay"></div>
  <div class="relative z-10 max-w-7xl mx-auto px-5 text-center">
    <p class="sl gp mb-4">Roof Repair</p>
    <h1 class="font-display font-black tracking-tightest mb-5" style="font-family:'Barlow Condensed',sans-serif;font-size:clamp(3rem,6vw,5rem);line-height:.92;letter-spacing:-.01em;color:#1A1A1A">
      ROOF REPAIR SERVICES<br/><span class="gt">IN TAMPA BAY.</span>
    </h1>
    <p style="color:#1A1A1A;font-size:1.1rem;line-height:1.75;font-weight:600;max-width:640px;margin:0 auto 1rem">
      Roof repair in Tampa Bay typically costs $350 to $1,500 depending on the damage. Happy Roof provides same-day emergency response with a 48-hour guarantee across Hillsborough, Pinellas, and Pasco counties. Licensed FL #CCC1337380.
    </p>
    <p style="color:#1A1A1A;font-size:.95rem;line-height:1.8;max-width:600px;margin:0 auto 1rem;border-left:3px solid #E6A817;padding-left:1.25rem">
      Here's what most roofers won't tell you: 60% of the 'repairs' we see were done wrong the first time by another contractor. A bad patch doesn't just fail. It hides the real problem until the damage is 3x worse. That's why we don't just fix the leak. We find out why it's leaking.
    </p>
    <p class="max-w-2xl mx-auto" style="color:#555555;font-size:1.05rem;line-height:1.75">
      When your roof is leaking, damaged, or compromised, you need a contractor who shows up fast, gives you an honest assessment, and does the job right. Happy Roof provides professional roof repairs across Tampa Bay with a 48-hour emergency response, backed by our up to 15-year workmanship warranty on qualifying repairs.
    </p>
    <p class="max-w-2xl mx-auto mt-4" style="color:#777;font-size:.88rem;line-height:1.75">
      Roof repair in Tampa Bay typically costs between $350 and $1,500 depending on the extent of damage. Happy Roof (FL License #CCC1337380) offers emergency tarping within 48 hours, leak detection, shingle and flashing replacement, soffit and fascia repair, and full storm damage restoration with insurance claim assistance. Serving Tampa, Clearwater, St. Petersburg, and surrounding areas. Free inspections. Call (813) 595-7663.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- INFO STRIP -->
<div style="background:#FFFFFF;border-top:2px solid #E6A817;border-bottom:1px solid #E0E0E0;padding:.85rem 0">
  <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-5">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-center gap-x-8 gap-y-2 font-display font-bold text-sm tracking-widest" style="color:#1A1A1A;text-transform:uppercase;font-family:'Barlow Condensed',sans-serif">
      <span>48hr Emergency Response</span>
      <span style="color:#E6A817">&middot;</span>
      <span>CCC1337380</span>
      <span style="color:#E6A817">&middot;</span>
      <span>Insurance Claim Help</span>
      <span style="color:#E6A817">&middot;</span>
      <span style="color:#3B9FD9">(813) 595-7663</span>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- FAST, HONEST INTRO -->
<section class="py-16" style="background:#FFFFFF">
  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-5 text-center">
    <p class="sl gt mb-3">Overview</p>
    <h2 style="font-family:'Barlow Condensed',sans-serif;font-weight:800;font-size:clamp(2rem,4vw,3rem);line-height:.95;color:#1A1A1A;letter-spacing:-.01em;margin-bottom:1.25rem">FAST, HONEST ROOF REPAIRS</h2>
    <p style="color:#555555;font-size:1.05rem;line-height:1.75;margin-bottom:1rem">
      When something goes wrong with your roof, waiting isn't really an option. Between Tampa Bay's heat and a storm season that doesn't take many breaks, even a small leak could become a much bigger problem in a short amount of time.
    </p>
    <p style="color:#555555;font-size:1.05rem;line-height:1.75">
      Happy Roof handles everything from emergency repairs and storm damage to leaks. Learn more about our roof repair services below.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- SERVICES OVERVIEW HEADER -->
<section class="pt-16 pb-4" style="background:#FFFFFF">
  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-5 text-center">
    <p class="sl gt mb-3">Services</p>
    <h2 style="font-family:'Barlow Condensed',sans-serif;font-weight:800;font-size:clamp(2rem,4vw,3rem);line-height:.95;color:#1A1A1A;letter-spacing:-.01em;margin-bottom:1rem">OUR PROFESSIONAL ROOF REPAIR SERVICES</h2>
    <p style="color:#555555;font-size:1rem;line-height:1.75;max-width:700px;margin:0 auto">
      We repair residential and commercial roofs across Tampa Bay, including single-family homes, rental properties, and commercial buildings.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- EMERGENCY REPAIRS -->
<section class="py-16" style="background:#FFFFFF">
  <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-5">
    <div class="grid lg:grid-cols-2 gap-14 items-start">
      <div>
        <p class="sl gt mb-3">Emergency Service</p>
        <h2 style="font-family:'Barlow Condensed',sans-serif;font-weight:800;font-size:clamp(2rem,4vw,3rem);line-height:.95;color:#1A1A1A;letter-spacing:-.01em;margin-bottom:1.5rem">EMERGENCY ROOF REPAIR</h2>
        <p style="color:#555555;font-size:1rem;line-height:1.75;margin-bottom:1.5rem">
          Whether a storm tears off shingles or a branch goes through the decking, we respond to emergency calls seven days a week and can typically have a crew on-site within 24 to 48 hours, usually the same day. We may use heavy-duty tarping or temporary patching to help stabilize your roof while a permanent solution is worked out.
        </p>
        <p style="color:#555555;font-size:1rem;line-height:1.75;margin-bottom:1.5rem">
          Once the immediate problem is contained, we'll perform a thorough inspection to assess the full scope of damage and give you a written estimate for the permanent repair. If the damage is covered by insurance, we'll also be sure to document everything your adjuster will need and can meet them on-site. For a detailed action plan, read our guide on <a href="/blog/emergency-roof-repair-what-to-do" style="color:#3B9FD9;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600">what to do when you have an emergency roof leak</a>.
        </p>
        <p style="color:#555555;font-size:1rem;line-height:1.75">
          Do not wait for water damage to spread. Call <a href="tel:8135957663" class="call-tracking-number" style="color:#3B9FD9;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600">(813) 595-7663</a> now, we answer 7 days a week.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="space-y-4">
        <div class="scard p-6">
          <div class="check"><div class="check-dot"><svg width="10" height="10" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#E6A817" stroke-width="3"><path d="M20 6L9 17l-5-5"/></svg></div><div><strong style="font-family:'Barlow Condensed',sans-serif;font-weight:700;font-size:1.05rem">Emergency Tarping</strong><p style="color:#555555;font-size:.9rem;line-height:1.6;margin-top:.25rem">Heavy-duty tarps secured to prevent further water intrusion. We use proper anchoring methods that protect your roof while keeping your home dry.</p></div></div>
        </div>
        <div class="scard p-6">
          <div class="check"><div class="check-dot"><svg width="10" height="10" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#E6A817" stroke-width="3"><path d="M20 6L9 17l-5-5"/></svg></div><div><strong style="font-family:'Barlow Condensed',sans-serif;font-weight:700;font-size:1.05rem">Temporary Patching</strong><p style="color:#555555;font-size:.9rem;line-height:1.6;margin-top:.25rem">Quick patches for punctures, holes, and exposed decking. Stops active leaks while you decide on permanent repair options.</p></div></div>
        </div>
        <div class="scard p-6">
          <div class="check"><div class="check-dot"><svg width="10" height="10" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#E6A817" stroke-width="3"><path d="M20 6L9 17l-5-5"/></svg></div><div><strong style="font-family:'Barlow Condensed',sans-serif;font-weight:700;font-size:1.05rem">Insurance Documentation</strong><p style="color:#555555;font-size:.9rem;line-height:1.6;margin-top:.25rem">We photograph all damage, provide detailed reports, and meet with your adjuster on-site to support your claim.</p></div></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- LEAK DETECTION -->
<section class="py-20" style="background:#F7F7F7">
  <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-5">
    <div class="text-center mb-14">
      <p class="sl gt mb-3">Leak Detection</p>
      <h2 style="font-family:'Barlow Condensed',sans-serif;font-weight:800;font-size:clamp(2rem,4vw,3rem);line-height:.95;color:#1A1A1A;letter-spacing:-.01em;margin-bottom:1rem">LEAK DETECTION &amp; DIAGNOSIS</h2>
      <p style="color:#555555;font-size:1rem;line-height:1.75;max-width:700px;margin:0 auto">
        Water on your ceiling doesn't always mean the leak is directly above it. In fact, it can travel along rafters and sheathing and show up several feet from where it actually entered. At Happy Roof, we typically start with a visual inspection of the full roof surface, and for leaks that don't present visually we may use controlled water testing to isolate the entry point. After the diagnosis, you'll always receive a written report with photos and a repair plan with transparent pricing.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="grid md:grid-cols-3 gap-8">
      <div class="scard p-8">
        <div style="width:52px;height:52px;border-radius:14px;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;background:rgba(230,168,23,.1);margin-bottom:1rem">
          <svg width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#E6A817" stroke-width="2"><circle cx="11" cy="11" r="8"/><path d="m21 21-4.35-4.35"/></svg>
        </div>
        <h3 style="font-family:'Barlow Condensed',sans-serif;font-weight:800;font-size:1.35rem;color:#1A1A1A;margin-bottom:.75rem">Visual Roof Inspection</h3>
        <p style="color:#555555;font-size:.95rem;line-height:1.7">
          We start with a comprehensive visual inspection of your entire roof surface, checking for missing, cracked, or curling shingles, damaged flashing, compromised sealant, and signs of wear around penetrations like vents, pipes, and skylights. We also inspect your attic from the inside, looking for daylight penetration, moisture stains, and mold growth.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="scard p-8">
        <div style="width:52px;height:52px;border-radius:14px;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;background:rgba(230,168,23,.1);margin-bottom:1rem">
          <svg width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#E6A817" stroke-width="2"><path d="M12 2.69l5.66 5.66a8 8 0 1 1-11.31 0z"/></svg>
        </div>
        <h3 style="font-family:'Barlow Condensed',sans-serif;font-weight:800;font-size:1.35rem;color:#1A1A1A;margin-bottom:.75rem">Water Testing</h3>
        <p style="color:#555555;font-size:.95rem;line-height:1.7">
          For leaks that are difficult to pinpoint visually, we use controlled water testing to isolate the entry point. By systematically wetting specific areas of the roof while monitoring the interior, we can identify exactly where water is penetrating, even when the stain on your ceiling is several feet from the actual source.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="scard p-8">
        <div style="width:52px;height:52px;border-radius:14px;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;background:rgba(230,168,23,.1);margin-bottom:1rem">
          <svg width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#E6A817" stroke-width="2"><path d="M14 2H6a2 2 0 0 0-2 2v16a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h12a2 2 0 0 0 2-2V8z"/><polyline points="14 2 14 8 20 8"/><line x1="16" y1="13" x2="8" y2="13"/><line x1="16" y1="17" x2="8" y2="17"/></svg>
        </div>
        <h3 style="font-family:'Barlow Condensed',sans-serif;font-weight:800;font-size:1.35rem;color:#1A1A1A;margin-bottom:.75rem">Detailed Repair Report</h3>
        <p style="color:#555555;font-size:.95rem;line-height:1.7">
          After diagnosis, you receive a detailed written report with photos documenting the damage, the identified leak source(s), and our recommended repair plan with pricing. If the damage is covered by insurance, this report serves as supporting documentation for your claim. No surprises, no guesswork.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- SHINGLE REPLACEMENT & FLASHING REPAIR -->
<section class="py-20" style="background:#FFFFFF">
  <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-5">
    <div class="grid lg:grid-cols-2 gap-14 items-start">
      <div>
        <p class="sl gt mb-3">Shingle Repair</p>
        <h2 style="font-family:'Barlow Condensed',sans-serif;font-weight:800;font-size:clamp(2rem,4vw,3rem);line-height:.95;color:#1A1A1A;letter-spacing:-.01em;margin-bottom:1.5rem">SHINGLE REPLACEMENT &amp; REPAIR</h2>
        <p style="color:#555555;font-size:1rem;line-height:1.75;margin-bottom:1.5rem">
          Even a small area of exposed decking, whether it's caused by missing or cracked shingles, can let in enough water to cause mold and interior damage within a few weeks in Tampa Bay's climate.
        </p>
        <p style="color:#555555;font-size:1rem;line-height:1.75;margin-bottom:1.5rem">
          We carry Owens Corning and other major-brand shingles in a range of colors and profiles, and we do our best to match what's already on your roof. If your shingles are discontinued or weathered enough that a close match isn't possible, we'll tell you upfront and discuss options, including a partial re-slope if that's what it takes to get a clean result.
        </p>
        <p style="color:#555555;font-size:1rem;line-height:1.75">
          Plus, every shingle repair includes an inspection of the underlayment and decking underneath. If there's moisture damage or rot beneath the surface, we'll address it before putting any new material down.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p class="sl gt mb-3">Flashing Repair</p>
        <h2 style="font-family:'Barlow Condensed',sans-serif;font-weight:800;font-size:clamp(2rem,4vw,3rem);line-height:.95;color:#1A1A1A;letter-spacing:-.01em;margin-bottom:1.5rem">FLASHING REPAIR &amp; REPLACEMENT</h2>
        <p style="color:#555555;font-size:1rem;line-height:1.75;margin-bottom:1.5rem">
          The metal strips that seal joints around chimneys, vents, skylights, valleys, and wall-to-roof transitions take a lot of abuse from Florida's heat and humidity, and if they corrode and pull away from the surface, water can find a way in pretty quickly.
        </p>
        <p style="color:#555555;font-size:1rem;line-height:1.75;margin-bottom:1.5rem">
          We repair and replace all types of flashing, including step flashing, counter flashing, valley flashing, drip edge, pipe boots, and chimney flashing. We use corrosion-resistant aluminum and galvanized steel and seal every repair with high-quality roofing sealant.
        </p>
        <p style="color:#555555;font-size:1rem;line-height:1.75">
          Every flashing repair we perform is mechanically fastened to code. We do not use roof cement as a substitute for proper flashing installation, a common shortcut that leads to callbacks and repeat leaks.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- STORM DAMAGE -->
<section class="py-20" style="background:#F7F7F7">
  <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-5">
    <div class="text-center mb-14">
      <p class="sl gt mb-3">Storm Damage</p>
      <h2 style="font-family:'Barlow Condensed',sans-serif;font-weight:800;font-size:clamp(2rem,4vw,3rem);line-height:.95;color:#1A1A1A;letter-spacing:-.01em;margin-bottom:1rem">STORM DAMAGE REPAIRS &amp; INSURANCE ASSISTANCE</h2>
      <p style="color:#555555;font-size:1rem;line-height:1.75;max-width:700px;margin:0 auto">
        After a storm, acting quickly is one of the best ways to protect both your home and your insurance claim. We can assess and repair everything from wind and hail to debris and tree damage on both residential and commercial roofs. Every storm inspection includes photo documentation and a written damage report. We work with all major Florida homeowners and commercial property insurers, and we can meet with your adjuster on-site to make sure nothing gets missed or underpaid.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
