<!-- REPAIR VS REPLACE -->
<section class="py-20" style="background:#FFFFFF">
  <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-5">
    <div class="text-center mb-14">
      <p class="sl gt mb-3">Decision Guide</p>
      <h2 style="font-family:'Barlow Condensed',sans-serif;font-weight:800;font-size:clamp(2rem,4vw,3rem);line-height:.95;color:#1A1A1A;letter-spacing:-.01em;margin-bottom:1rem">HOW DO I KNOW IF MY ROOF NEEDS A REPAIR OR A FULL REPLACEMENT?</h2>
      <p style="color:#555555;font-size:1rem;line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin:0 auto 1rem">
        Generally speaking, a repair usually makes the most sense when the damage is isolated, and your roof is under 15 to 20 years old. Good candidates for repair typically include flash failure around one vent or a small area of storm damage. A replacement starts to make more sense when your roof is showing widespread wear or when you've had the same area repaired more than once.
      </p>
      <p style="color:#555555;font-size:1rem;line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin:0 auto">
        If we come out and find that a repair is the right call, that's what we'll tell you, even when a replacement would make us more money. At the end of the day, we'd rather earn your trust and your next call than oversell you on work you don't need. You can also read our full guide on the <a href="/blog/signs-you-need-roof-replacement" style="color:#3B9FD9;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600">warning signs that indicate a full replacement</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-8">
      <div class="scard p-8">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Barlow Condensed',sans-serif;font-weight:800;font-size:1.35rem;color:#1A1A1A;margin-bottom:1rem">
          <span style="color:#3B9FD9">REPAIR</span> Makes Sense When...
        </h3>
        <ul style="color:#555555;font-size:.95rem;line-height:1.7;list-style:none;padding:0;margin:0">
          <li style="margin-bottom:.75rem;padding-left:1.5rem;position:relative"><span style="position:absolute;left:0;color:#E6A817;font-weight:700">+</span> Damage is isolated to one area or a few shingles</li>
          <li style="margin-bottom:.75rem;padding-left:1.5rem;position:relative"><span style="position:absolute;left:0;color:#E6A817;font-weight:700">+</span> Your roof is less than 15 years old</li>
          <li style="margin-bottom:.75rem;padding-left:1.5rem;position:relative"><span style="position:absolute;left:0;color:#E6A817;font-weight:700">+</span> There is a single, identifiable leak point</li>
          <li style="margin-bottom:.75rem;padding-left:1.5rem;position:relative"><span style="position:absolute;left:0;color:#E6A817;font-weight:700">+</span> Flashing around one penetration has failed</li>
          <li style="padding-left:1.5rem;position:relative"><span style="position:absolute;left:0;color:#E6A817;font-weight:700">+</span> The decking underneath is still solid</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="scard p-8">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Barlow Condensed',sans-serif;font-weight:800;font-size:1.35rem;color:#1A1A1A;margin-bottom:1rem">
          <span style="color:#3B9FD9">REPLACE</span> Makes Sense When...
        </h3>
        <ul style="color:#555555;font-size:.95rem;line-height:1.7;list-style:none;padding:0;margin:0">
          <li style="margin-bottom:.75rem;padding-left:1.5rem;position:relative"><span style="position:absolute;left:0;color:#3B9FD9;font-weight:700">+</span> Your roof is 20+ years old with widespread wear</li>
          <li style="margin-bottom:.75rem;padding-left:1.5rem;position:relative"><span style="position:absolute;left:0;color:#3B9FD9;font-weight:700">+</span> Multiple areas are leaking or showing damage</li>
          <li style="margin-bottom:.75rem;padding-left:1.5rem;position:relative"><span style="position:absolute;left:0;color:#3B9FD9;font-weight:700">+</span> Decking is rotted or delaminated in multiple spots</li>
          <li style="margin-bottom:.75rem;padding-left:1.5rem;position:relative"><span style="position:absolute;left:0;color:#3B9FD9;font-weight:700">+</span> You have had repeated repairs in the last few years</li>
          <li style="padding-left:1.5rem;position:relative"><span style="position:absolute;left:0;color:#3B9FD9;font-weight:700">+</span> Insurance is covering storm damage to the full roof</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

