<!-- DIY vs PRO -->
<section class="py-20" style="background:#F5F5F5;border-top:1px solid #E5E5E5;border-bottom:1px solid #E5E5E5">
  <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-5">
    <div class="text-center mb-12">
      <p class="sl gp mb-3">One Call Saves a Fall</p>
      <h2 style="font-family:'Barlow Condensed',sans-serif;font-weight:800;font-size:clamp(2rem,4vw,3rem);line-height:.95;color:#1A1A1A;letter-spacing:-.01em">DIY REPAIRS VS. WHEN TO CALL A PRO</h2>
      <p style="color:#555555;font-size:1.05rem;line-height:1.75;margin-top:1rem;max-width:720px;margin-left:auto;margin-right:auto">
        The single biggest risk in DIY roofing isn't the repair, it's the fall. The <a href="https://www.cdc.gov/falls/index.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="color:#3B9FD9;text-decoration:underline">CDC documents</a> over 150,000 ladder-fall ER visits every year, and Florida's heat-brittled shingles plus fragile tile make walking a roof more dangerous than most homeowners expect.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
      <div style="background:#FFFFFF;border:1px solid #E0E0E0;border-radius:16px;padding:1.75rem;box-shadow:0 4px 20px -6px rgba(0,0,0,.06)">
        <p style="font-family:'Barlow Condensed',sans-serif;font-weight:800;font-size:1rem;color:#059669;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;margin-bottom:1rem">Safe From the Ground or an Eave-Anchored Ladder</p>
        <ul style="color:#555555;font-size:.95rem;line-height:1.75;padding-left:1.25rem;list-style:disc">
          <li>Clean gutters and downspouts (the #1 hidden leak cause)</li>
          <li>Trim overhanging branches with a pole saw</li>
          <li>Photograph the roof after every named storm, same angles, date-stamped</li>
          <li>Attic check twice a year for water stains, daylight, or musty smell</li>
          <li>Reseal a first-floor porch-roof sealant bead with shingle-safe caulk</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#FFFFFF;border:1px solid #E0E0E0;border-radius:16px;padding:1.75rem;box-shadow:0 4px 20px -6px rgba(0,0,0,.06)">
        <p style="font-family:'Barlow Condensed',sans-serif;font-weight:800;font-size:1rem;color:#DC2626;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;margin-bottom:1rem">Always Call a Licensed Roofer For</p>
        <ul style="color:#555555;font-size:.95rem;line-height:1.75;padding-left:1.25rem;list-style:disc">
          <li>Any leak repair (80% of leaks start at flashing; DIY caulking hides the source)</li>
          <li>Shingle or tile replacement on the roof plane</li>
          <li>Anything near chimneys, skylights, vents, or valleys (warranty-sensitive)</li>
          <li>Storm damage inspection with insurance implications</li>
          <li>Two-story homes or roof pitches above 6:12</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="text-center mt-10">
      <p style="color:#1A1A1A;font-family:'Barlow Condensed',sans-serif;font-weight:700;font-size:1.15rem;letter-spacing:.02em;margin-bottom:1rem">
        Rule of thumb: if the fix requires walking the roof, call us.
      </p>
      <a href="/contact" class="btn-t" style="display:inline-block">Get a Free Inspection</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

