        Does Happy Roof help with roof insurance claims?
        <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#1A1A1A" stroke-width="2.5"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg>
      </button>
      <div class="faq-answer">
        <div class="faq-answer-inner">Yes. Happy Roof provides full insurance claim assistance for storm damage and other covered roof repairs. We document all damage with photos and detailed reports, meet with your insurance adjuster on-site, and help ensure your claim is processed fairly. We work with all major Florida homeowners insurance carriers. We never inflate damage reports or pressure you into unnecessary work.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="faq-item">
      <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false" onclick="this.setAttribute('aria-expanded',this.getAttribute('aria-expanded')==='true'?'false':'true');this.nextElementSibling.classList.toggle('open')">
        How do I know if my roof needs a repair or a full replacement?
        <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#1A1A1A" stroke-width="2.5"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg>
      </button>
      <div class="faq-answer">
        <div class="faq-answer-inner">Generally, if the damage is isolated to a small area - missing shingles, a single leak point, damaged flashing around one penetration - a repair is the most cost-effective solution. If your roof is over 15-20 years old, has widespread damage, multiple leak points, or significant decking deterioration, a full replacement is usually the better long-term investment. Happy Roof provides honest assessments. We will never recommend a replacement when a repair will do the job.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="faq-item">
      <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false" onclick="this.setAttribute('aria-expanded',this.getAttribute('aria-expanded')==='true'?'false':'true');this.nextElementSibling.classList.toggle('open')">
        Do you offer a warranty on roof repairs?
        <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#1A1A1A" stroke-width="2.5"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg>
      </button>
      <div class="faq-answer">
        <div class="faq-answer-inner">Yes. Qualifying repairs come with our written workmanship warranty of up to 15 years, which covers our labor and installation. Not every repair qualifies at the same level; for example, emergency tarping is different from a permanent shingle or flashing repair, but we'll always tell you exactly what's covered before work starts.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="faq-item">
      <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false" onclick="this.setAttribute('aria-expanded',this.getAttribute('aria-expanded')==='true'?'false':'true');this.nextElementSibling.classList.toggle('open')">
        How much does a roof repair cost in Tampa Bay?
        <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#1A1A1A" stroke-width="2.5"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg>
      </button>
      <div class="faq-answer">
        <div class="faq-answer-inner">Minor repairs like replacing a few shingles or sealing a small leak typically run $300 to $800. More involved repairs (e.g., flashing replacement, multiple leak sources, storm damage restoration) typically fall between $1,000 and $3,500 or more depending on scope. Happy Roof provides free inspections and written estimates with no hidden fees. Call <a href="tel:8135957663" class="call-tracking-number" style="color:#3B9FD9;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600">(813) 595-7663</a> for a personalized quote.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="faq-item">
      <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false" onclick="this.setAttribute('aria-expanded',this.getAttribute('aria-expanded')==='true'?'false':'true');this.nextElementSibling.classList.toggle('open')">
        Can you repair a TPO or flat roof?
        <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#1A1A1A" stroke-width="2.5"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg>
      </button>
      <div class="faq-answer">
        <div class="faq-answer-inner">Yes. Happy Roof repairs all flat roof systems including TPO, EPDM, modified bitumen, and built-up roofing. Common flat roof repairs include seam re-welding, puncture patching, flashing replacement, and ponding water correction. We also repair leaks around rooftop HVAC units, pipes, and drains. Call <a href="tel:8135957663" class="call-tracking-number" style="color:#3B9FD9;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600">(813) 595-7663</a> for a free inspection.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="faq-item">
      <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false" onclick="this.setAttribute('aria-expanded',this.getAttribute('aria-expanded')==='true'?'false':'true');this.nextElementSibling.classList.toggle('open')">
        What can I do to prevent roof leaks?
        <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#1A1A1A" stroke-width="2.5"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg>
      </button>
      <div class="faq-answer">
        <div class="faq-answer-inner">Most roof leaks start in relatively predictable places. Inspecting your flashing twice a year, particularly around any chimneys, vents, skylights, and places where the roof meets the wall, can help you catch a lot of problems on the early side. Other efforts include:<br/><br/><strong>Keep gutters clear</strong> to prevent water from backing up under the drip edge.<br/><br/><strong>Trim branches that hang over the roof</strong> to reduce debris and potential abrasion.<br/><br/><strong>Check for lifted or missing shingles</strong> after any named storm to have a chance of addressing smaller issues before they become more serious ones.<br/><br/>Plus, a professional inspection once a year, which we offer for free, is the single most effective thing you can do to stay ahead of it. Call <a href="tel:8135957663" class="call-tracking-number" style="color:#3B9FD9;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600">(813) 595-7663</a>.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="faq-item">
      <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false" onclick="this.setAttribute('aria-expanded',this.getAttribute('aria-expanded')==='true'?'false':'true');this.nextElementSibling.classList.toggle('open')">
        Which roof repairs are safe to DIY, and when should I call a pro?
        <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#1A1A1A" stroke-width="2.5"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg>
      </button>
      <div class="faq-answer">
        <div class="faq-answer-inner">Roof access is where most DIY roofing goes wrong. The CDC documents over 150,000 ladder-fall ER visits every year in the US, and Florida shingle heat plus tile fragility make walking a roof more dangerous than most homeowners realize.<br/><br/><strong>Safe to DIY</strong> (from the ground or an eave-anchored ladder only, never the roof plane):<br/>1. Clear gutters and downspouts, the #1 cause of hidden leaks. A gutter scoop and a stable ladder against the eave is all you need.<br/>2. Trim overhanging branches with a pole saw from the ground to keep limbs off the shingles and reduce debris.<br/>3. Photograph the roof after every named storm from the ground, same angles, in the same order. Insurance loves date-stamped 'before' photos.<br/>4. Attic check twice a year: flashlight, look for water stains on the underside of decking, daylight through nail holes, wet insulation, or musty smell.<br/>5. Reseal exposed sealant on ground-accessible sections only, like a first-floor porch roof, using a shingle-safe sealant. Never attempt from a ladder above 10 feet or on the main roof plane.<br/><br/><strong>Call a licensed roofer for:</strong> any leak repair (80% of leaks start at flashing, and DIY caulking hides the source while the deck rots underneath); any shingle or tile replacement on a walkable roof; any work around chimneys, skylights, plumbing vents, or valleys (all warranty-sensitive); any tile repair (cracked tiles under foot are the injury pattern we see most); storm damage inspection with insurance implications (an untrained eye misses hail bruising and wind-lifted seals that a licensed inspector documents for a claim); and any repair on a two-story home or roof pitch above 6:12.<br/><br/>Rule of thumb: if the fix requires walking the roof plane, you need a licensed roofer. Happy Roof offers free inspections at <a href="tel:8135957663" class="call-tracking-number" style="color:#3B9FD9;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600">(813) 595-7663</a>. One call saves a fall.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

